do $seed$ declare source jsonb; candidate jsonb:=$payload${"code": "R-005", "disposition": "revise", "revision": "2026-10-15.1", "content": {"skill": "reading", "title": "Testing a hybrid working week", "scope": "Foundation reading practice; not a full IELTS paper", "instructions": "Answer every question using only the passage. For True/False/Not Given: True agrees, False contradicts, Not Given is not established. For gaps use ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage.", "passage": "A. This fictional case study follows a small design company. Its manager introduced a six-week trial in which employees worked at home for two days and in the office for three. The aim was to combine quiet individual work with opportunities for face-to-face discussion. Employees still had to attend agreed meetings.\n\nB. At home, several employees reported that they could finish detailed drawings with fewer interruptions. Others found it difficult to work in a shared living space. The company lent screens to employees who needed them, but it did not assume that equipment alone would solve every problem.\n\nC. On office days, the team held planning meetings and reviewed designs together. A new employee particularly valued being able to ask a colleague a quick question. However, employees said that travelling into the office only to join online meetings was frustrating. The manager therefore moved most shared activities onto the same office days.\n\nD. At the end of the trial, the company compared completed projects, employee comments and meeting attendance. It did not use time spent online as its only measure of useful work. The manager kept a flexible arrangement and planned a further review after three months. The trial provided information about this company; it did not prove that the same timetable would suit every employer.", "questions": [{"n": 1, "type": "multiple_choice", "question": "What was the main aim of the trial?", "options": ["To remove all meetings", "To make every employee work alone", "To reduce the number of projects", "To combine focused work and shared discussion"], "key": "D", "evidence": "A: combine quiet individual work with opportunities for face-to-face discussion"}, {"n": 2, "type": "multiple_choice", "question": "What difficulty did some employees have at home?", "options": ["A shared living space made work difficult", "The office had too many screens", "All meetings were cancelled", "They could not contact any colleagues"], "key": "A", "evidence": "B: difficult to work in a shared living space"}, {"n": 3, "type": "true_false_ng", "question": "The company judged useful work only by time spent online.", "options": ["True", "False", "Not Given"], "key": "False", "evidence": "D: It did not use time spent online as its only measure"}, {"n": 4, "type": "true_false_ng", "question": "Every employee preferred working at home.", "options": ["True", "False", "Not Given"], "key": "Not Given", "evidence": "Some benefits and difficulties are reported; no universal preference is stated"}, {"n": 5, "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The manager planned another review after _____ months.", "key": ["three"], "evidence": "D: a further review after three months"}, {"n": 6, "type": "multiple_choice", "question": "What limitation does the final paragraph acknowledge?", "options": ["The trial included no employee comments", "Its findings may not suit every employer", "No projects were completed", "Meeting attendance was not examined"], "key": "B", "evidence": "D: did not prove that the same timetable would suit every employer"}], "authorship": "Brains Heist AI-assisted revision; human review pending", "sources": []}, "changes": ["Re-authored passage and evidence-bound questions", "Balanced MCQ positions with plausible distractors", "Contiguous numbering and explicit response limits", "Removed unsupported statistics and explanations"], "blockers": ["Human editorial/key review", "Source and reuse-rights review", "Originality and exposure-family review", "Delivery and scoped pilot checks"], "material_type": "ielts_reading_set", "material_id": "3", "source_snapshot": {"id": 3, "slug": "working-from-home", "level": "beginner", "title": "Working from Home", "is_active": true, "questions": [{"id": 8, "body": "What accelerated the trend of working from home?", "set_id": 3, "options": ["The COVID-19 pandemic", "Technology advances", "Company policies", "Economic recession"], "explanation": "The passage begins by stating \"The COVID-19 pandemic accelerated a trend.\"", "question_type": "multiple_choice", "correct_answer": "The COVID-19 pandemic", "question_order": 1}, {"id": 9, "body": "What is mentioned as an advantage of working from home?", "set_id": 3, "options": ["Eliminating daily commute", "Higher salary", "Better equipment", "More meetings"], "explanation": "The passage states \"Employees save time and money by eliminating their daily commute.\"", "question_type": "multiple_choice", "correct_answer": "Eliminating daily commute", "question_order": 2}, {"id": 10, "body": "What approach are many organizations adopting?", "set_id": 3, "options": ["Hybrid models", "Full remote work", "Return to office", "Four-day work week"], "explanation": "The passage concludes that \"many organizations are adopting hybrid models.\"", "question_type": "multiple_choice", "correct_answer": "Hybrid models", "question_order": 3}], "created_at": "2025-11-17T12:58:50.309363+00:00", "description": "A general training passage about the advantages and challenges of remote work.", "display_code": "R-005", "est_band_max": 6, "est_band_min": 4.5, "passage_text": "The COVID-19 pandemic accelerated a trend that had been slowly developing for years: working from home. What was once a rare perk offered by progressive companies became an overnight necessity for millions of workers worldwide.\n\nWorking from home offers several advantages. Employees save time and money by eliminating their daily commute. They often report higher productivity due to fewer office distractions and interruptions. Parents particularly appreciate the flexibility to manage childcare responsibilities alongside their work duties.\n\nHowever, remote work also presents challenges. Many people struggle with work-life balance when their home becomes their office. The lack of face-to-face interaction can lead to feelings of isolation and disconnect from colleagues. Technical issues and inadequate home office setups can hinder productivity.\n\nAs we move forward, many organizations are adopting hybrid models that combine remote and office work. This approach aims to capture the benefits of both arrangements while minimizing their respective drawbacks.", "required_tier": "free", "duration_minutes": 15, "originality_label": null}, "review_status": "pending_human_review", "human_approval": null, "revision_sha256": "5b855f48c85749e3a834fdaabf87714fda3a6310aea1059c789e962354141c29"}$payload$::jsonb; begin
