do $seed$ declare source jsonb; candidate jsonb:=$payload${"code": "W-005", "disposition": "revise", "revision": "2026-10-15.1", "content": {"skill": "writing", "title": "Environmental Responsibility", "scope": "Writing practice; example response is not a band guarantee", "test_type": "academic", "task_number": 2, "minimum_words": 250, "suggested_minutes": 40, "prompt": "Some people think that environmental problems should be solved on a global scale, while others believe individual responsibility is more important. Discuss both views and give your opinion. Write at least 250 words.", "model_answer": "Environmental problems cross borders, yet many of the actions that create them happen in individual homes and communities. Some people therefore favour international solutions, while others place more responsibility on individuals. I believe that both are necessary, although governments have a particular duty to make responsible choices practical.\n\nGlobal cooperation is important because countries share natural systems. Pollution released in one place can affect people and wildlife elsewhere, and a single country cannot protect an entire ocean by acting alone. International agreements can establish common goals and encourage governments to coordinate their efforts. They can also help countries share knowledge and resources. However, an agreement has limited value if it is not supported by effective action within each country.\n\nIndividuals also influence environmental outcomes through everyday decisions. People can reduce unnecessary waste, repair useful items and choose lower-impact travel when a suitable option exists. These actions can support broader changes by showing demand for more sustainable products and services. A household that plans meals carefully, for example, may throw away less food. Such behaviour is worthwhile even though it cannot solve every environmental problem on its own.\n\nThe difficulty is that personal choice depends partly on the systems available. It is unreasonable to expect someone to use public transport if there is no reliable service. Similarly, households cannot recycle materials that local facilities do not accept. Governments and businesses should therefore provide the infrastructure and clear information that make useful individual action possible. Responsibility should reflect both a person's choices and their real opportunities.\n\nIn conclusion, international cooperation can address problems that extend beyond national borders, while individual action supports change in daily life. These approaches work best together. Placing all responsibility on either governments or individuals would overlook an important part of the solution.", "teacher_notes": "Review the response against the relevant four Writing criteria. The model is one possible response, not the only answer and not a certified band. Check claims, organisation, language and task coverage separately.", "authorship": "Brains Heist AI-assisted revision; human review pending", "model_word_count": 295, "sources": []}, "changes": ["Completed the fragment with an original full response", "Normalized task number, test type, word minimum and timing units", "Model clearly labelled as an example, without a band claim"], "blockers": ["Human editorial/key review", "Source and reuse-rights review", "Originality and exposure-family review", "Delivery and scoped pilot checks"], "material_type": "ielts_writing_task", "material_id": "3", "source_snapshot": {"id": 3, "slug": "environmental-responsibility", "title": "Environmental Responsibility", "prompt": "Some people think that environmental problems should be solved on a global scale, while others believe individual responsibility is more important. Discuss both views and give your opinion. Write at least 250 words.", "is_active": true, "task_type": "task2", "created_at": "2025-11-17T16:32:23.268633+00:00", "bands_target": "6.0-8.0", "display_code": "W-005", "required_tier": "prime_prep_user", "sample_answer": "Environmental degradation is one of the most pressing challenges facing humanity today...", "originality_label": null}, "review_status": "pending_human_review", "human_approval": null, "revision_sha256": "142cfc702f281fbce1316351cff4fe0a526f27d2d3269ce1690085d7899ecfd1"}$payload$::jsonb; begin
